- If multiple people speak simultaneously, note it as [crosstalk].
- Identify speakers by their Zoom display name AND by voice. If the Zoom label is wrong or two people share one camera, distinguish them by voice.
- In the end of the prompt you will find a Zoom transcript. Use it to define speakers, but note that Zoom knows nothing about people sharing one camera.

Transcribe rules:
- Use short first names as speaker labels (Иван, Мария, etc.).
- Include timestamps at the start of each speaker's turn in [MM:SS] format.
- Transcribe in the original language of the speech (do not translate).
- Clean up speech for readability: remove filler words, false starts, and repetitions. Preserve meaning and natural tone, but make it easy to read.
- The transcribed text from the Zoom transcript is low quality in terms of words recognition, don't rely on it.

